# The offset-law table of the joint certificate: entries 0 to 3327

The entries `g_{0}, …, g_{3327}` of the offset-law table of the joint certificate, in blocks
of `256` consecutive entries: `jointCertGBlock i` packs `g_{256 i}, …, g_{256 i + 255}` as `64`-bit
lanes (the last block stops at `g_6198`).

## Main definitions

* `CollatzPosDens.jointCertGBlock0`: entries `0` to `255`.
* `CollatzPosDens.jointCertGBlock1`: entries `256` to `511`.
* `CollatzPosDens.jointCertGBlock2`: entries `512` to `767`.
* `CollatzPosDens.jointCertGBlock3`: entries `768` to `1023`.
